n. Any shut in or significant curtailment in gathering system or transportation, processing or refining-facility capacity, or an inability to obtain favorable terms for delivery of the crude oil and natural gas produced from Sitio’s acreage, could reduce Sitio’s E&P operators’ ability to market the production from Sitio’s properties and have a material adverse effect on Sitio’s financial condition, results of operations and cash flows. Sitio’s E&P operators’ access to transportation options and the prices Sitio or its E&P operators receive can also be affected by federal and state regulation—including regulation of crude oil, natural gas and NGLs production, transportation and pipeline safety—as well by general economic conditions and changes in supply and demand.
